### Base URL
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api

### An admin token. Sign in with adminAuthAPI.rest and paste it here —
### every /sizeCharts route is behind the admin guard.
@token = PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN

### A chart id, from the list below.
@chartId = PASTE_CHART_ID


### ============================================================
### SIZE CHARTS — F-06
### ============================================================
###
### The tables the storefront prints beside every size picker. Shop-wide
### rather than per category: one chart per fit, and a shopper picks
### between them with a tab.
###
### 014_create_size_charts.sql seeds Normal Fit and Slim Fit, so a fresh
### database already answers the two reads below with the shop's real
### charts.


### ============================================================
### PUBLIC — what a shopper reads
### ============================================================
###
### No token. Six columns: the id, the print position and the published
### flag are the admin's business and are not in the payload at all.

GET {{baseUrl}}/storefront/getSizeCharts


### ============================================================
### Get All Size Charts (admin — published or not)
### ============================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/sizeCharts/getSizeCharts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### Get Size Chart by ID
### ============================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/sizeCharts/getSizeChartById/{{chartId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### Create Size Chart — a new fit
### ============================================================
###
### `columns` are keys, and the set is closed — see
### config/size_chart.policy.js. "size" must be first.
###
### A null measurement is a blank cell, printed as a dash. Do not send 0
### for "not stated": zero is a measurement.

POST {{baseUrl}}/sizeCharts/createSizeChart
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fit": "Special Dress",
  "title": "Special dress — gowns and heavy anarkalis",
  "unit": "in",
  "columns": ["size", "bust", "waist", "hip", "length"],
  "rows": [
    { "size": "S",  "bust": 36, "waist": 30, "hip": 39, "length": 54 },
    { "size": "M",  "bust": 38, "waist": 32, "hip": 41, "length": 55 },
    { "size": "L",  "bust": 40, "waist": 34, "hip": 43, "length": 56 },
    { "size": "XL", "bust": 42, "waist": 36, "hip": 45, "length": null }
  ]
}


### ============================================================
### Update Size Chart — a full replace
### ============================================================
###
### Send the whole chart. There is no partial update of a measurement
### grid: dropping a column and clearing it are different edits, and a
### per-field patch could not tell them apart.
###
### `position` and `active` are optional and keep whatever the chart
### already had — correcting a hip measurement must not move the tab or
### republish a chart the shop had taken down.

PUT {{baseUrl}}/sizeCharts/updateSizeChart/{{chartId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fit": "Special Dress",
  "title": "Special dress — gowns, heavy anarkalis and occasion wear",
  "unit": "in",
  "columns": ["size", "bust", "waist", "hip", "length"],
  "rows": [
    { "size": "S",  "bust": 36, "waist": 30, "hip": 39, "length": 54 },
    { "size": "M",  "bust": 38, "waist": 32, "hip": 41, "length": 55 },
    { "size": "L",  "bust": 40, "waist": 34, "hip": 43, "length": 56 },
    { "size": "XL", "bust": 42, "waist": 36, "hip": 45, "length": 57 }
  ]
}


### ============================================================
### Hide a chart from the storefront (and put it back)
### ============================================================

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/sizeCharts/setSizeChartActive/{{chartId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "active": false
}


### ============================================================
### Reorder — the order the tabs appear in
### ============================================================
###
### Every chart, in the order they should print. A partial list is
### refused rather than half-applied: it would renumber the ones named
### from 1 and leave the rest sharing positions with them.

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/sizeCharts/reorderSizeCharts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ids": [
    "PASTE_FIRST_CHART_ID",
    "PASTE_SECOND_CHART_ID"
  ]
}


### ============================================================
### Delete Size Chart
### ============================================================
###
### Permanent, and the measurements are kept nowhere else. Hiding is
### what setSizeChartActive is for.

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/sizeCharts/deleteSizeChart/{{chartId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ============================================================
### Validation — these should all fail with 400
### ============================================================

### A first column that is not "size"
POST {{baseUrl}}/sizeCharts/createSizeChart
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fit": "Broken",
  "title": "Columns out of order",
  "columns": ["bust", "size"],
  "rows": [{ "size": "M", "bust": 38 }]
}


### A measurement key the columns do not declare
POST {{baseUrl}}/sizeCharts/createSizeChart
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fit": "Broken",
  "title": "Row carries a column the chart has not got",
  "columns": ["size", "bust"],
  "rows": [{ "size": "M", "bust": 38, "hip": 40 }]
}


### A fit that already exists — 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/sizeCharts/createSizeChart
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fit": "slim fit",
  "title": "Case does not make it a different fit",
  "columns": ["size", "bust"],
  "rows": [{ "size": "M", "bust": 38 }]
}
